Amendment No. 4 §3 conditions:
(a) counterparts signed by the Loan Parties, the Agent and the Required Lenders;
(b) officer's certificate on 3(d)-(e) and a CFO solvency certificate;
(c) payment of fees due on the effective date and of expenses invoiced at least 1 Business Day before;
(d) reps true in all material respects;
(e) no Default or Event of Default.
Section 4.01 (original closing conditions) is [Reserved] in the conformed copy.

7.01 events of default:
(a) principal / LC reimbursement: no grace;
(b) interest and fees: 5 Business Days;
(d) breach of 5.02(a), 5.03 (existence), 5.10, 5.16 or Article 6: immediate;
(e) other covenants: 30 days after notice;
(f)/(g) cross-payment-default and cross-acceleration to Material Indebtedness above $25,000,000, after grace periods;
(h) involuntary insolvency: 60 days;
(l) judgments above $25,000,000 that remain undischarged and unstayed for 30 consecutive days;
(n) Change in Control;
(o)-(p) guarantee, Loan Document or Lien invalidity.

Assignments (not to Loan Parties or their Affiliates) need consent, not to be unreasonably withheld or delayed, from:
- the Parent Borrower: not needed for assignments to a Lender, an Affiliate of a Lender or an Approved Fund, or during an Event of Default; deemed given unless it objects within 10 Business Days;
- the Agent: not needed for assignment of a Commitment to an existing Lender with a Commitment, an Affiliate of a Lender or an Approved Fund;
- each Issuing Bank.
Minimum assignment is $5,000,000, except assignments to a Lender or Lender Affiliate or of the entire remaining amount. Participations are permitted under 10.04(c).

Standard provisions:
- Increased costs (2.12);
- Taxes (2.14);
- Mitigation and replacement of Lenders, including Defaulting and Non-Consenting Lenders (2.16(b));
- Defaulting Lender provisions (2.17), including reallocation and cash collateral;
- EU/UK bail-in acknowledgment (10.19).

Amendment No. 4 §4 authorises the Agent to agree further revisions to three security documents:
- Omnibus Security Agreement: security supplements semi-annually or on request, instead of within 60 days;
- Dutch Omnibus Pledge §8.1: 'commercially reasonable efforts' standard for Schedule 5 updates;
- Taiwan Accounts Pledge §5.2: remittance and withdrawal notices only on Agent request, at most once a quarter absent an Event of Default.
§5 extends the Schedule I post-closing perfection deadlines to 120 days after the effective date, with no retroactive default. Schedule I includes Taiwan control agreements and pledge acknowledgements, and Australia, UK, Philippines and Netherlands items. §5 also waives the German moveable-asset transfer requirement.

7.03 waterfall (after an Event of Default, at the Agent's election or the Required Lenders' direction):
(1) Agent and Issuing Bank fees, indemnities and expenses;
(2) Lender fees and expenses;
(3)-(4) Protective Advances, interest then principal;
(5) interest on Loans and LC Disbursements;
(6) ratably: principal, LC Disbursements, LC cash cover (103%/105%), and Specified Cash Management and Swap obligations owed to Lenders or their Affiliates;
(7) other Approved Counterparty swaps;
(8) other Obligations;
(9) any remainder to the Loan Party.
